    <id>https://doi.org/10.1093/restud/rdag122</id>
    <title>Meritocracy and Homophily in Collegial Organizations</title>
    <updated>2026-11-17T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Paul-Henri Moisson, Jean Tirole</name>
    </author>
    <content>&lt;b&gt;Review of Economic Studies&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;In collegial organizations, homophily jeopardizes the recruitment of the most talented (“meritocracy”). We analyze the dynamics and welfare properties of an organization whose incumbent members coopt new ones in a forward-looking manner. We identify organizations in which meritocracy is likely to give way to favoritism and entrenchment, and investigate policy interventions (such as affirmative action, quality-based or diversity-based funding, discretionary overruling of majority decisions, blind hiring processes) and their unintended consequences.</content>
