    <id>https://doi.org/10.1287/opre.2025.1654</id>
    <title>Joint Assortment Planning and Inventory Control Under General Choice Models</title>
    <updated>2026-11-26T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <author>
      <name>Qiaochu Fu, Woonghee Tim Huh, Yanzhi Li, Tongwen Wu</name>
    </author>
    <content>&lt;b&gt;Operations Research&lt;/b&gt; &lt;br&gt;Constant-Factor Algorithms for Dynamic Assortment and Inventory PlanningRetailers must decide which products to stock and how much inventory to carry when customers may substitute to other products after their preferred items sell out. In “Joint Assortment Planning and Inventory Control Under General Choice Models,” Fu, Huh, Li, and Wu develop a polynomial-time framework for this problem under a broad class of customer choice models and stochastic demand. Their approach combines a fluid relaxation with a new static-allocation method to obtain the first constant-factor approximation guarantees for several general choice models, including the Markov chain choice model and mixtures of multinomial logit models. Under the widely used multinomial logit model, the algorithm guarantees at least 0.25 of the optimal expected revenue, improving the previous best guarantee of about 0.194. The guarantees become stronger when inventory capacity is relatively large or when customer arrivals follow deterministic or Poisson distributions.</content>
